Files in this part should run as follows:
Open PyMOL, then run the script with the command:

```
run /path/to/pymol_script.py
```

This script will set up a PyMOL scene for the structure, and save the session in the specified directory.
Make sure to adjust the path to the script as needed.

Other option is to run the script directly from the command line using:

```
python scripts/pymol_script.py
```

To install PyMOL, you can use the following command:

```
conda install -c conda-forge pymol-open-source  
```

No need to run the script in a cluster, unless high-resolution rendering is desired.